.TH LOG-SUMMARY-NORMALIZE 1 "2026-10-22" "SASD Freeware 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
log-summary-normalize \- convert complete M7 log aggregate reports to JSON Lines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B log-summary-normalize
.B --source
.I journal-summary|syslog-summary|ssh-auth-summary|auth-event-summary
.RB [ --input " FILE|-" ]
.RB [ --format " tsv|null" ]
.br
.B log-summary-normalize
.RB [ --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Converts a complete, bounded TSV or NUL summary report from one named SASD
log utility into a stable JSONL schema. Never reads raw log content as a source,
contacts services, or changes system state. Validation completes before output.
.SS Schema
Each JSON line contains schema=sasd.log-summary.v1, scope=source_summary,
source, type, category, priority (integer or null), and numeric count. The
TOTAL row has type=total. The complete source vocabulary and input column
order are checked; duplicate/missing rows and inconsistent totals are rejected.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --source " NAME"
Required. Must be exactly one of the four supported source tool names.
.TP
.BI --input " FILE|-"
Read one report from a regular file or stdin (default). Named symlinks rejected.
.TP
.BI --format " tsv|null"
Require the upstream tabular TSV output (default) or its --null form.
.TP
.B --help
Show usage.
.TP
.B --version
Show tool version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: valid complete report, no UNKNOWN. 1: valid report containing UNKNOWN.
2: invalid CLI. 3: incomplete/malformed/oversized input or missing dependency.
Fatal input errors never produce partial JSONL output.
.SH SECURITY AND LIMITATIONS
Maximum 8192 bytes, 16 report rows, counts up to 50000. All output source
names and categories are fixed constants. Raw log content, host and identity
data are not emitted. Reports from different tools may count the SAME
underlying log records. Never sum them as a distinct-event count. There is
no event-level timestamp, de-duplication, temporal correlation or claim of
verified security incidents in this schema.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR journal-summary (1),
.BR syslog-summary (1),
.BR ssh-auth-summary (1),
.BR auth-event-summary (1)
.SH AUTHOR
SASD Freeware contributors.
